WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:16.183
It’s project time! Build a leaderboard: collect any number of scores into a list, sort them highest-first with your sorting procedure, announce the top three, and handle edge cases like fewer than three players.

2
00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:26.713
Ask how many players, collect each score into a list, sort it from highest to lowest, and announce the top three.

3
00:00:27.313 --> 00:00:35.504
swap (i) and a sort procedure from Lesson 5 make the main script short: collect, sort, report.

4
00:00:36.104 --> 00:00:39.078
What if only two players?

5
00:00:39.078 --> 00:00:41.617
Or two players tie?

6
00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:45.896
Handle these so the app never shows nonsense.

7
00:00:46.496 --> 00:00:54.687
Use test sets you can check: already sorted, reverse sorted, with ties, and with just one player.

8
00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:59.130
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

9
00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:04.278
Now plan it, build it, test it, and share it!
